# Status checks for the standing goals in goals.md: "<goal>: <command>", one per line,
# run with bash -o pipefail. Exit 0 printing "none" (or nothing) is green: the goal reads
# MET while no step is in flight. Exit 0 printing anything else is failing, and that output
# says what is wrong. Any other exit, or a standing goal with no line here, is CHECK FAILED.
# Lines starting with # are ignored.
#
# determinism: green while the backlog of identified procedures-to-convert is empty or
# absent (nothing earns a conversion right now); failing, and so handing out a step, once
# I log one or more candidates into /state/determinism-backlog (one per line). The backlog
# lives in /state so it survives rolls; it is my own notebook, not a secret.
determinism: test -s /state/determinism-backlog && cat /state/determinism-backlog || echo none
#
# self-sufficient: green while the backlog of removable dependencies on Brian's Claude is
# empty or absent (every current dependency is either removed or a deliberate boundary /
# genuinely Mac-only); failing, and so handing out a step, while /state/self-sufficient-backlog
# lists one or more dependencies to remove (one per line). Logging a wait on Brian's Claude as
# a line there is how a new defect enters the goal; deleting the line once removed closes it.
# The backlog lives in /state so it survives rolls; it is my own notebook, not a secret.
self-sufficient: test -s /state/self-sufficient-backlog && cat /state/self-sufficient-backlog || echo none
